Wang Zhao 王詔, Gentleman for Literature and Chief Supervising Secretary of the Office of Scrutiny for Rites [metropolitan graduate of the renxu year (1442)].

Sealing Officials (彌封官):
Li Chun 李春, Grand Master forThe Splendid Happiness and Right Vice Minister of Rites in charge of the Court of Imperial Entertainments [tribute scholar (gongshi)];
Yang Xun 楊詢, Grand Master of Palace Accord and Chief Minister of the Court of State Ceremonial [National University student (jiansheng)];
Yu Qian 余謙, Secondary Grand Master of the Center and Chief Minister of the Court of the Imperial Stud [cultivated talent (xiucai)];
Ling Xin 凌信, Grand Master for Proper Consultation and Chief Minister of the Seals Office [government student (shengyuan)];
Yuan Kai 袁愷, Gentleman for Literature and Chief Supervising Secretary of the Office of Scrutiny for War [metropolitan graduate of the jiaxu year (1454)];
Pan Li 潘禮, Gentleman for Manifest Service and Supervising Secretary in charge of the Office of Scrutiny for Revenue [metropolitan graduate of the gengchen year (1460)].

Custodians of Papers (掌卷官):
Peng Jiao 彭教, Senior Compiler of the Hanlin Academy [metropolitan graduate of the jiashen year (1464)];
Liu Jian 劉健, Junior Compiler of the Hanlin Academy and Gentleman for Literature [metropolitan graduate of the gengchen year (1460)];
Jin Shen 金紳, Gentleman for Literature and Chief Supervising Secretary of the Office of Scrutiny for Justice [metropolitan graduate of the jiaxu year (1454)];
Huang Zhen 黃甄, Gentleman for Manifest Service and Right Supervising Secretary of the Office of Scrutiny for Works [metropolitan graduate of the jiaxu year (1454)].

Patrolling Officials (巡綽官):
Yuan Bin 袁彬, General of Illustrious Courage and Assistant Military Commissioner of the Embroidered-Uniform Guard;
Jiao Shou 焦壽, General Who Cherishes the Distant and Vice Commander of the Embroidered-Uniform Guard;
Zhao Neng 趙能, General of Bright Prestige and Assistant Commander of the Embroidered-Uniform Guard;
Zhai Tong 翟通, General Who Cherishes the Distant and Vice Commander of the Imperial Bodyguard Front Guard (Jinwu qian wei);
Chen Gang 陳綱, General of Illustrious Courage and Commander of the Imperial Bodyguard Rear Guard (Jinwu hou wei).

